  "body": "## What changed\n- The machine list and the post list come from a scan of their folders. They no longer come from the fixed `MACHINES` and `BUILTINS` tables.\n- A file in the folder that has no table entry is listed as a file entry. It uses the existing `LoadMachineFile` and `SelectPostFile` commands.\n- A table entry shows only if its file is present. A removed file does not leave an entry.\n- The Refresh buttons scan the folder again (`posting::rescan`). The machine page and the post picker have a Refresh button.\n- A malformed file does not stop the scan. It is listed with its own refusals.\n- A document that needs a missing post or machine is still refused by name (#2319).\n- The MCP machine-name list uses the same scan.\n- The folder listing is `camcraft_post::data_dir::list_files`. The scan is `crates/app/src/posting_scan.rs`.\n\n## Root cause\nThe lists were built from `BUILTINS` and `MACHINES` in `crates/app/src/posting_files.rs`. The UI pickers and `machine/library.rs` `builtins()` read those tables. No code read the folder.\n\n## Pinning tests\n`crates/app/tests/folder_lists.rs`:\n- `the_machine_list_follows_its_folder`\n- `the_post_list_follows_its_folder`\n- `a_missing_folder_lists_nothing_and_says_why`\n- `the_process_lists_read_the_shipped_folders`\n\n## Readings\n- The tests `folder_lists`, `machine_edit`, `machine_library` and `shipped_from_disk` pass. The `camcraft-ui` lib tests that match `machine` pass (88).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The real GUI was not started.\n- The full quick gate did not finish on this head. It was stopped after two failures that are now fixed (the default machine file `3axis-vmc.mch` showed as an extra). The targeted suites above ran on the final head.\n\n## Decisions\nSee `docs/decisions/2380-folder-scan-lists.md`. A file that was read once and removed later still posts from the cached text until restart.\n\nEffort: medium\nChangelog: Machine and post lists now follow their folders: new files appear, removed files disappear, and Refresh scans again.\n\nFixes #2380\n\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
